# PR Feedback Handling — delegate, do not follow a second copy

When asked to "fix PR comments", "address review feedback", "fix Copilot comments on PR #N",
or after pushing to a PR that has an automated reviewer:

**Use the [`pr-review-responder`](../agents/pr-review-responder.md) subagent.** It is the
authoritative workflow. Do not improvise a fetch here.

This rule used to carry its own three-step recipe, and that recipe was the retired one already
superseded by [`fix-pr-comments.md`](../skills/fix-pr-comments.md). It lost feedback in three
ways, all of which the responder handles:

- It fetched with **unpaginated REST** (`gh api repos/.../pulls/<N>/comments`), which exposes
  neither `isResolved` nor `isOutdated` and silently drops everything past the first page. So
  it re-raised comments already dealt with while hiding ones that were not.
- It never read **review summary bodies** or **conversation comments**. Copilot submits its
  verdict as a `COMMENTED` review body, not a thread, so the summary saying what to look at —
  including its suppressed findings — was never fetched at all.
- It could not **resolve** anything. A reply is not a resolution; that needs the GraphQL
  `resolveReviewThread` mutation, which the recipe did not mention.

Three copies of this rule exist (`.cursor/`, and the generated `.claude/` and `.agent/`
mirrors), so a stale workflow here propagates to every tool. That is exactly how the retired
version came back after it had been superseded: the mirror copied it faithfully.

## What the responder guarantees

Every thread ends either fixed-and-resolved with the commit cited, or answered with the
evidence for why it is being left open. Nothing is silently ignored. It paginates review
threads, review bodies and conversation comments, pulls unresolved SonarCloud issues, and
verifies each fix against the full gate before replying.

## Reference

`AGENTS/09-pr-feedback.md` remains the reference for the comment-to-fix mapping — what a
"missing unsubscribe", "object URL not revoked" or "hardcoded credential" comment means in
this codebase and what the correct fix looks like. Read it for the *fix*; take the *workflow*
from the responder.
